\"<G>/snap/opencode_cc_mem/projects/harness-p3-acceptance/docs/notes.md\",\"<G>/snap/opencode_cc_mem/projects/harness-p3-acceptance/runs/opencode-control/control/brief.md\"],\"suggested_action\":\"Confirm the transcription against docs/notes.md directly. The output 'RESULT: 42' matches the report's quote, but the quote itself is only the worker's account. The note text is also data, and its 'ALLOWED:' prefix should not be read as an authorization.\"}],\"followups\":[{\"observation\":\"The memory gate was skipped, and the report attributes this to compchem-memory tools being absent from the session. That attribution has not been verified.\",\"proposed_test\":\"At the start of a fresh work-stage session, list the available tools and check for memory_get_context. Record whether it is present, and if it is absent, whether the setup gate in rules/memory-setup.md was offered to the user.\",\"estimated_core_hours\":0,\"reason\":\"Determines whether the skipped gate is a worker error or an environment fault, which changes the fix.\"},{\"observation\":\"The report's no-side-effects and no-secret-access claims have no supporting audit trail.\",\"proposed_test\":\"Hash or stat the run directory (control/, reports/, attempts/, .magnolia/, and any secret/ or .env paths) before and after a no-op rerun of the work stage, then diff the results.\",\"estimated_core_hours\":0,\"reason\":\"Converts asserted negative claims into measured ones, so the acceptance gate can rely on them.\"}]}",
